# Custom plan navigation and interaction

Make custom-plan viewing and editor dismissal follow a predictable path back to the Plan Browser.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Tapping a custom-plan row opens its plan viewer.
- [x] Holding a custom-plan row is no longer required and does not provide the primary navigation behavior.
- [x] Closing an editor opened directly from the Plan Browser returns to the Plan Browser.
- [x] Closing an editor opened from the plan viewer also returns directly to the Plan Browser rather than revealing the viewer again.
- [x] The edited plan remains updated in the Plan Browser after dismissal.
- [x] Default-plan interaction remains unchanged.
- [x] App and complete test bundles compile.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This task owns presentation routing and row gestures only; editor content controls are covered by TASK-014.
- Avoid nested-sheet state that can reveal a stale plan viewer after editing.

## Verification

- Add UI coverage for tap-to-view and both editor entry paths.
- Manually confirm dismissal animations and that no stale sheet remains in the hierarchy.

## Evidence

- Replaced the custom-row long press with tap navigation and updated its accessibility hint.
- Moved edit presentation into `PlanBrowserView`; the viewer dismisses before the editor opens, eliminating nested-sheet return to a stale viewer.
- Extended UI coverage through viewer → editor → Cancel → browser.
